1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,008
Summers in Japan are *brutally* hot, aren’t they? Today’s video: *How to Survive a Japanese Summer!*

2
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: The Dangers of Extreme Heat Days

3
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:14,919
Did you check the weather forecast?

4
00:00:14,942 --> 00:00:17,390
No, I didn’t.

5
00:00:17,413 --> 00:00:19,580
What’s wrong?

6
00:00:19,603 --> 00:00:23,336
They’re saying it’s going to be *scorching* today.

7
00:00:23,359 --> 00:00:25,759
How hot are we talking?

8
00:00:25,783 --> 00:00:29,150
Some places will hit over 40°C (104°F).

9
00:00:29,173 --> 00:00:33,632
40°C?! That’s *insane*.

10
00:00:33,656 --> 00:00:37,658
Yeah, it’s *dangerously* hot.

11
00:00:37,681 --> 00:00:40,568
They even came up with a new word for it, didn’t they?

12
00:00:40,591 --> 00:00:44,724
Yep—*‘Extreme Heat Day.’*

13
00:00:44,747 --> 00:00:46,547
What does that mean?

14
00:00:46,570 --> 00:00:52,570
It’s when the temperature goes above 40°C.

15
00:00:52,593 --> 00:00:55,160
*‘Extreme Heat Day’*—easy to remember!

16
00:00:55,183 --> 00:00:59,316
Gifu and Aichi already hit 40°C.

17
00:00:59,339 --> 00:01:01,473
What about Tokyo?

18
00:01:01,495 --> 00:01:05,664
Tokyo’s gonna be over 36°C (97°F).

19
00:01:05,687 --> 00:01:08,854
Walking outside is gonna be *rough*.

20
00:01:08,877 --> 00:01:12,443
The Japan Meteorological Agency is warning everyone.

21
00:01:12,466 --> 00:01:14,600
What are they saying?

22
00:01:14,623 --> 00:01:19,029
They’re telling people to *keep the AC running*.

23
00:01:19,053 --> 00:01:22,619
I’m worried about the electric bill… but I’ll use it.

24
00:01:22,642 --> 00:01:27,257
Protecting your life is what matters most.

25
00:01:27,281 --> 00:01:29,749
Staying hydrated is key too, right?

26
00:01:29,772 --> 00:01:33,639
Yeah—drink *before* you get thirsty.

27
00:01:33,662 --> 00:01:36,629
I’ll go grab some sports drinks.

28
00:01:36,651 --> 00:01:40,585
And wear a hat if you go outside!

29
00:01:40,608 --> 00:01:43,408
Should I use a parasol too?

30
00:01:43,431 --> 00:01:47,406
Yeah—guys use them all the time now.

31
00:01:47,429 --> 00:01:50,100
I’ll buy one too!

32
00:01:50,124 --> 00:01:53,757
Taking breaks in cool places is important.

33
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:56,313
Like convenience stores or malls?

34
00:01:56,336 --> 00:01:59,772
Exactly—it’s called *‘Cool Share.’*

35
00:01:59,795 --> 00:02:03,829
There are *emergency cool spots* all over the city.

36
00:02:03,852 --> 00:02:06,385
Don’t push yourself—take it easy.

37
00:02:06,408 --> 00:02:09,288
Got it—I’ll be careful.

38
00:02:09,311 --> 00:02:13,113
If you start feeling sick, *rest immediately*.

39
00:02:13,137 --> 00:02:15,004
Understood!

40
00:02:15,027 --> 00:02:17,360
Checking in on others is important too.

41
00:02:17,383 --> 00:02:20,550
Let’s tell our friends and family.

42
00:02:20,573 --> 00:02:23,239
I’ll text them right now!

43
00:02:23,262 --> 00:02:26,831
*Seriously*—watch out for heatstroke.

44
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:29,466
I will!

45
00:02:29,490 --> 00:02:31,189
Thanks for the reminder!

46
00:02:31,212 --> 00:02:34,183
Let’s power through today safely!

47
00:02:34,206 --> 00:02:36,981
Yeah—let’s do this!

48
00:02:37,005 --> 00:02:46,014
You can download today’s script from the description and top comment!

49
00:02:46,014 --> 00:02:47,514
Scene 2: How to Use Air Conditioners and Fans Effectively

50
00:02:47,514 --> 00:02:50,772
Is your room cool enough?

51
00:02:50,796 --> 00:02:55,037
Yes, I have the air conditioner on.

52
00:02:55,061 --> 00:02:58,336
What temperature is it set to?

53
00:02:58,359 --> 00:03:01,926
I've set it to 28°C.

54
00:03:01,949 --> 00:03:05,582
28°C is a great temperature.

55
00:03:05,605 --> 00:03:08,972
I'm also using a fan with it.

56
00:03:08,995 --> 00:03:13,415
Using a fan really cools you down, doesn't it?

57
00:03:13,438 --> 00:03:16,813
The breeze feels so refreshing.

58
00:03:16,837 --> 00:03:20,244
Do you leave the air conditioner on at night too?

59
00:03:20,267 --> 00:03:24,347
Yes, I keep it on until morning.

60
00:03:24,371 --> 00:03:28,108
It can be risky if you turn it off midway.

61
00:03:28,132 --> 00:03:32,065
Don’t you wake up with a headache in the morning?

62
00:03:32,088 --> 00:03:35,544
I make sure the airflow doesn’t hit me directly.

63
00:03:35,568 --> 00:03:38,534
I adjust the direction of the wind.

64
00:03:38,557 --> 00:03:41,524
Have you cleaned the filter recently?

65
00:03:41,547 --> 00:03:44,387
I cleaned it last week.

66
00:03:44,411 --> 00:03:48,621
Cleaning it makes the room cool faster.

67
00:03:48,645 --> 00:03:51,678
It also helps save on electricity bills.

68
00:03:51,701 --> 00:03:55,268
Closing the curtains is effective too.

69
00:03:55,291 --> 00:03:59,158
I use blackout curtains.

70
00:03:59,182 --> 00:04:03,215
It’s great because the sunlight doesn’t come in.

71
00:04:03,238 --> 00:04:06,438
The room temperature doesn’t rise as much.

72
00:04:06,461 --> 00:04:10,341
Do you stay hydrated indoors too?

73
00:04:10,364 --> 00:04:13,900
I keep water on my desk.

74
00:04:13,923 --> 00:04:17,325
It’s reassuring to have water always available.

75
00:04:17,349 --> 00:04:20,955
I drink even if I’m not sweating.

76
00:04:20,978 --> 00:04:24,511
You can still get heatstroke indoors, after all.

77
00:04:24,535 --> 00:04:27,635
I see it on the news all the time.

78
00:04:27,658 --> 00:04:30,658
Managing indoor conditions is so important.

79
00:04:30,681 --> 00:04:33,481
I’ll teach my family about it too.

80
00:04:33,504 --> 00:04:37,118
Let’s remind each other to stay safe.

81
00:04:37,142 --> 00:04:40,790
Yes, I’ll be careful with my health.

82
00:04:40,813 --> 00:04:43,847
Let’s enjoy a comfortable summer!

83
00:04:43,870 --> 00:04:46,604
Yes, thank you!

84
00:04:46,628 --> 00:04:53,733
You can review today’s video with the link in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

85
00:04:53,733 --> 00:04:55,233
Scene 3: Heatstroke Prevention Items

86
00:04:55,233 --> 00:04:59,433
Did you go to the drugstore?

87
00:04:59,456 --> 00:05:03,731
Yes, I went today.

88
00:05:03,754 --> 00:05:07,987
Did you buy any heatstroke prevention items?

89
00:05:08,011 --> 00:05:11,662
Yes, I bought quite a few things.

90
00:05:11,685 --> 00:05:14,452
What did you get?

91
00:05:14,475 --> 00:05:18,042
I bought a cooling spray.

92
00:05:18,065 --> 00:05:21,431
The kind you spray over your clothes?

93
00:05:21,454 --> 00:05:25,821
Yes, it feels so cool!

94
00:05:25,844 --> 00:05:30,183
Did you also get some sweat wipes?

95
00:05:30,206 --> 00:05:34,261
I bought the ones with menthol.

96
00:05:34,285 --> 00:05:37,928
They leave you feeling refreshed.

97
00:05:37,952 --> 00:05:40,718
It feels great!

98
00:05:40,741 --> 00:05:44,075
Do you have any salt tablets?

99
00:05:44,098 --> 00:05:47,593
Yes, I bought some salt candies.

100
00:05:47,616 --> 00:05:51,995
You need salt when you sweat.

101
00:05:52,019 --> 00:05:55,238
I carry it in my pocket.

102
00:05:55,261 --> 00:05:58,629
It's best to have it with water.

103
00:05:58,653 --> 00:06:02,301
That's really informative.

104
00:06:02,325 --> 00:06:05,137
Should I also apply the ice sheet?

105
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:09,494
I bought a cooling sheet for the back of my neck.

106
00:06:09,517 --> 00:06:13,761
Cooling your neck chills your whole body, doesn't it?

107
00:06:13,784 --> 00:06:17,117
It worked right away!

108
00:06:17,140 --> 00:06:20,315
Do you also use a handheld fan?

109
00:06:20,339 --> 00:06:24,206
Yes, it's a rechargeable fan.

110
00:06:24,229 --> 00:06:27,962
You see a lot of people carrying them around town.

111
00:06:27,985 --> 00:06:31,483
Some fans even spray a fine water mist.

112
00:06:31,507 --> 00:06:34,910
That sounds so refreshing!

113
00:06:34,934 --> 00:06:39,227
There are so many different cooling gadgets these days.

114
00:06:39,250 --> 00:06:42,783
Just use whatever you like best!

115
00:06:42,806 --> 00:06:45,673
I carry it with me every day.

116
00:06:45,696 --> 00:06:48,896
You're so well-prepared!

117
00:06:48,919 --> 00:06:52,298
Because I want to sightsee safely.

118
00:06:52,321 --> 00:06:55,255
It sounds like you'll have a great time!

119
00:06:55,278 --> 00:06:59,250
Yes, I'll do my best to stay safe.

120
00:06:59,273 --> 00:07:00,773
Scene 4: Summer Hydration – Stay Cool with the Right Drinks

121
00:07:00,773 --> 00:07:05,106
What do you usually drink in the summer?

122
00:07:05,129 --> 00:07:08,463
I often drink cold barley tea.

123
00:07:08,486 --> 00:07:10,963
Barley tea is great!

124
00:07:10,986 --> 00:07:14,444
I like it because it's caffeine-free.

125
00:07:14,467 --> 00:07:17,345
It also contains minerals.

126
00:07:17,368 --> 00:07:20,601
Perfect for staying hydrated!

127
00:07:20,624 --> 00:07:23,710
Do you drink sports drinks too?

128
00:07:23,733 --> 00:07:27,867
Yes, I drink them when I sweat a lot.

129
00:07:27,890 --> 00:07:31,131
They contain sugar and salt.

130
00:07:31,155 --> 00:07:34,435
I dilute them with water to make them easier to drink.

131
00:07:34,458 --> 00:07:37,342
That makes them much more refreshing!

132
00:07:37,366 --> 00:07:41,532
I buy cold drinks at convenience stores.

133
00:07:41,555 --> 00:07:45,006
There are so many vending machines around the city.

134
00:07:45,030 --> 00:07:48,209
It's so convenient to buy drinks anywhere.

135
00:07:48,232 --> 00:07:51,432
Cold green tea is also delicious!

136
00:07:51,455 --> 00:07:54,022
You mean bottled green tea, right?

137
00:07:54,045 --> 00:07:57,012
Yes, it's so refreshing!

138
00:07:57,035 --> 00:08:00,435
What about sugary soft drinks?

139
00:08:00,458 --> 00:08:03,731
Drinking too much makes you thirstier.

140
00:08:03,754 --> 00:08:06,754
Water or tea is better.

141
00:08:06,777 --> 00:08:10,344
Have you heard of oral rehydration solutions?

142
00:08:10,367 --> 00:08:12,442
You mean OS-1?

143
00:08:12,465 --> 00:08:16,503
Yes, I drink it when I'm not feeling well.

144
00:08:16,527 --> 00:08:18,927
It's sold at pharmacies.

145
00:08:18,950 --> 00:08:22,150
It works wonders for heatstroke.

146
00:08:22,173 --> 00:08:24,549
I'll buy a bottle to keep on hand.

147
00:08:24,572 --> 00:08:27,605
What about the temperature of your drinks?

148
00:08:27,628 --> 00:08:30,828
Is drinking something too cold bad for you?

149
00:08:30,851 --> 00:08:33,885
It can upset your stomach.

150
00:08:33,908 --> 00:08:36,908
I also drink room-temperature beverages.

151
00:08:36,931 --> 00:08:40,464
It's best to drink in a way that's gentle on your body.

152
00:08:40,487 --> 00:08:43,520
Yes, I'll make sure to drink mindfully.

153
00:08:43,543 --> 00:08:46,310
The trick is to sip water regularly.

154
00:08:46,333 --> 00:08:49,566
Got it—I'll keep that in mind.

155
00:08:49,589 --> 00:08:51,089
Scene 5: The Convenience of Using a Parasol

156
00:08:51,089 --> 00:08:55,756
More and more people are using parasols these days.

157
00:08:55,779 --> 00:08:58,912
I use one too.

158
00:08:58,935 --> 00:09:02,502
Does it really make a difference?

159
00:09:02,525 --> 00:09:05,091
Absolutely!

160
00:09:05,115 --> 00:09:07,122
It keeps you so much cooler.

161
00:09:07,145 --> 00:09:10,884
It blocks direct sunlight, after all.

162
00:09:10,907 --> 00:09:13,719
It actually lowers how hot you feel.

163
00:09:13,742 --> 00:09:16,876
What kind of parasol do you use?

164
00:09:16,900 --> 00:09:20,467
A 100% UV-blocking parasol.

165
00:09:20,490 --> 00:09:23,767
That’s an amazing parasol!

166
00:09:23,790 --> 00:09:27,924
It’s foldable, so it’s easy to carry around.

167
00:09:27,947 --> 00:09:31,013
Is it an all-weather parasol?

168
00:09:31,036 --> 00:09:32,487
Yes, it is.

169
00:09:32,511 --> 00:09:35,280
You can use it on rainy days too.

170
00:09:35,303 --> 00:09:37,948
It’s so handy to have just one.

171
00:09:37,972 --> 00:09:41,013
I also use a handheld fan with it.

172
00:09:41,037 --> 00:09:44,204
Double the effect with a parasol and a fan!

173
00:09:44,226 --> 00:09:47,076
Walking becomes so much easier.

174
00:09:47,100 --> 00:09:51,381
When walking in the city, I pay attention to etiquette.

175
00:09:51,404 --> 00:09:53,446
What kind of etiquette?

176
00:09:53,470 --> 00:09:58,563
Be careful when opening your parasol in crowded places.

177
00:09:58,586 --> 00:10:02,120
Make sure it doesn’t hit anyone around you.

178
00:10:02,143 --> 00:10:06,543
On narrow streets, hold your parasol higher.

179
00:10:06,566 --> 00:10:09,808
Fold it when getting on a train.

180
00:10:09,831 --> 00:10:12,910
Put wet parasols in a bag.

181
00:10:12,934 --> 00:10:14,134
Yes, it is.

182
00:10:14,157 --> 00:10:16,596
Following etiquette is important.

183
00:10:16,619 --> 00:10:20,471
A quiet handheld fan is best.

184
00:10:20,494 --> 00:10:23,540
I use it in quiet mode.

185
00:10:23,563 --> 00:10:28,135
Avoid pointing the wind directly at people’s faces.

186
00:10:28,158 --> 00:10:31,598
Being considerate of others is key.

187
00:10:31,622 --> 00:10:34,677
It helps everyone stay comfortable.

188
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:37,535
I’ll use them with good manners.

189
00:10:37,559 --> 00:10:40,926
These are such handy and comfortable tools!

190
00:10:40,949 --> 00:10:43,317
I can’t live without them now.

191
00:10:43,340 --> 00:10:44,840
Scene 6: Cool Off with Indoor Sightseeing

192
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:49,855
It’s so hot outside—let’s explore indoors instead!

193
00:10:49,879 --> 00:10:52,046
Where should we go?

194
00:10:52,069 --> 00:10:55,469
Let’s visit an art museum in Ueno.

195
00:10:55,492 --> 00:10:58,868
Are museums cool inside?

196
00:10:58,891 --> 00:11:03,858
Yes, they maintain a steady temperature for the artwork.

197
00:11:03,881 --> 00:11:07,330
It’s cool and comfortable!

198
00:11:07,353 --> 00:11:10,920
You can quietly enjoy the paintings.

199
00:11:10,943 --> 00:11:13,509
What a wonderful plan!

200
00:11:13,532 --> 00:11:16,825
Aquariums are also a great option.

201
00:11:16,849 --> 00:11:19,716
Shinagawa Aquarium, you mean?

202
00:11:19,739 --> 00:11:23,825
Yes, we have a large aquarium here.

203
00:11:23,848 --> 00:11:27,532
Watching fish really cools you down, doesn’t it?

204
00:11:27,556 --> 00:11:30,189
There’s also a dolphin show!

205
00:11:30,212 --> 00:11:33,145
Are there seats where you might get splashed?

206
00:11:33,168 --> 00:11:36,982
Yes, the front rows will get you wet.

207
00:11:37,006 --> 00:11:39,473
That sounds refreshing!

208
00:11:39,496 --> 00:11:42,966
The basement of department stores is also a lot of fun.

209
00:11:42,989 --> 00:11:45,189
You mean the depachika?

210
00:11:45,212 --> 00:11:47,346
There’s so much food to try.

211
00:11:47,369 --> 00:11:50,908
You’ll find delicious cakes and traditional Japanese sweets.

212
00:11:50,931 --> 00:11:53,348
Can we try samples?

213
00:11:53,372 --> 00:11:56,461
Yes, some shops offer samples.

214
00:11:56,484 --> 00:12:00,752
Staying indoors means no sunburn either.

215
00:12:00,776 --> 00:12:03,776
And no sweating—so comfortable!

216
00:12:03,799 --> 00:12:06,399
Going to the movies is another great option.

217
00:12:06,422 --> 00:12:09,956
Japanese theaters are so clean and nice.

218
00:12:09,979 --> 00:12:12,746
I’ll grab some popcorn and enjoy the show.

219
00:12:12,769 --> 00:12:16,202
Indoor summer sightseeing is the best.

220
00:12:16,225 --> 00:12:19,592
On hot days, indoor spots are the way to go.

221
00:12:19,615 --> 00:12:22,415
Let’s plan our day out.

222
00:12:22,438 --> 00:12:25,205
Yes, I’m really looking forward to it!

223
00:12:25,228 --> 00:12:26,728
Scene 7: Beat the Summer Slump! Energizing Foods for a Refreshing Boost

224
00:12:26,728 --> 00:12:29,426
Feeling a bit sluggish from the summer heat?

225
00:12:29,449 --> 00:12:33,500
I do feel a little weighed down.

226
00:12:33,524 --> 00:12:36,357
Let’s recharge with the right foods!

227
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:39,039
What should we eat?

228
00:12:39,063 --> 00:12:41,997
Eel is a classic choice!

229
00:12:42,020 --> 00:12:45,199
It’s Unagi Day, after all!

230
00:12:45,222 --> 00:12:46,898
Yes, it is.

231
00:12:46,921 --> 00:12:50,288
Eating eel really gives you energy.

232
00:12:50,311 --> 00:12:53,606
Is it packed with vitamins?

233
00:12:53,629 --> 00:12:57,363
It’s rich in vitamins A and B.

234
00:12:57,386 --> 00:13:00,398
I love the smell of the sauce.

235
00:13:00,421 --> 00:13:02,990
It really makes the rice go down well!

236
00:13:03,013 --> 00:13:08,613
I’m also craving something cold—how about chilled Chinese noodles?

237
00:13:08,636 --> 00:13:12,270
The vinegar dressing makes it so refreshing!

238
00:13:12,293 --> 00:13:15,293
It comes with cucumber and ham on top.

239
00:13:15,316 --> 00:13:18,483
Light and easy to eat—perfect for summer.

240
00:13:18,506 --> 00:13:21,593
Somen noodles are another summer staple.

241
00:13:21,617 --> 00:13:24,664
Those thin, white noodles, right?

242
00:13:24,687 --> 00:13:27,860
You dip them in mentsuyu broth.

243
00:13:27,883 --> 00:13:31,918
Add some green onions or ginger for extra flavor.

244
00:13:31,942 --> 00:13:35,001
Ginger is great for your health too.

245
00:13:35,024 --> 00:13:37,513
It really wakes up your appetite!

246
00:13:37,537 --> 00:13:41,793
Pork is also high in vitamin B1.

247
00:13:41,816 --> 00:13:44,149
Let’s make some chilled shabu-shabu pork.

248
00:13:44,172 --> 00:13:47,585
Eating it with veggies is even better.

249
00:13:47,609 --> 00:13:50,175
Drizzle some sesame sauce on top.

250
00:13:50,198 --> 00:13:52,249
That sounds delicious!

251
00:13:52,272 --> 00:13:56,039
Let’s eat well and power through the summer!

252
00:13:56,062 --> 00:13:59,200
A balanced diet is key.

253
00:13:59,224 --> 00:14:02,390
I make sure to get plenty of sleep.

254
00:14:02,413 --> 00:14:05,380
That sounds like a healthy lifestyle.

255
00:14:05,403 --> 00:14:06,885
Yes, it is.

256
00:14:06,909 --> 00:14:08,642
I'll do my best!

257
00:14:08,665 --> 00:14:10,165
Scene 8: The Joy of Kakigori and Parfait / Enjoying Kakigori and Parfait

258
00:14:10,165 --> 00:14:15,532
Shall we go grab some cold sweets?

259
00:14:15,555 --> 00:14:18,209
Sounds great! What are you thinking of getting?

260
00:14:18,232 --> 00:14:21,234
Let's have kakigori!

261
00:14:21,257 --> 00:14:25,143
Japanese kakigori is so famous, isn't it?

262
00:14:25,167 --> 00:14:28,900
There's a shop where the ice is fluffy like snow.

263
00:14:28,923 --> 00:14:33,538
Fluffy ice? That sounds amazing!

264
00:14:33,561 --> 00:14:37,252
We'll drizzle matcha and red bean syrup on top.

265
00:14:37,276 --> 00:14:39,476
Oh, that's Uji Kintoki!

266
00:14:39,499 --> 00:14:42,899
Yep, and we'll add condensed milk too.

267
00:14:42,922 --> 00:14:45,522
It's going to be absolutely delicious.

268
00:14:45,545 --> 00:14:49,545
They also have syrups made from seasonal fruits.

269
00:14:49,568 --> 00:14:51,824
Like peach or strawberry?

270
00:14:51,847 --> 00:14:55,847
Yes, they use fresh fruit!

271
00:14:55,870 --> 00:14:58,870
This kakigori is pure luxury!

272
00:14:58,893 --> 00:15:02,101
There's also a café with amazing parfaits.

273
00:15:02,125 --> 00:15:04,496
Are you thinking of a melon parfait?

274
00:15:04,519 --> 00:15:07,996
Yes, they have these huge parfaits!

275
00:15:08,019 --> 00:15:11,275
And it comes with ice cream on top!

276
00:15:11,298 --> 00:15:14,594
It'll look so cute in photos!

277
00:15:14,618 --> 00:15:17,351
Perfect for Instagram!

278
00:15:17,374 --> 00:15:20,307
Did you make a reservation for the shop?

279
00:15:20,330 --> 00:15:24,064
Do we need to line up for popular places?

280
00:15:24,086 --> 00:15:27,520
A lot of shops give out numbered tickets.

281
00:15:27,543 --> 00:15:29,676
We should go early.

282
00:15:29,699 --> 00:15:33,332
Eating it in a cool room is the best.

283
00:15:33,355 --> 00:15:36,726
Doesn't it give you brain freeze?

284
00:15:36,750 --> 00:15:39,950
It's fine if you eat it slowly.

285
00:15:39,973 --> 00:15:42,307
Let's savor every bite.

286
00:15:42,330 --> 00:15:45,169
Let's treat ourselves with something sweet.

287
00:15:45,192 --> 00:15:47,691
Yes, let's go!

288
00:15:47,715 --> 00:15:49,215
Scene 9: How to Enjoy a Summer Festival / The Joys of a Summer Festival

289
00:15:49,215 --> 00:15:53,548
Want to go to a festival tonight?

290
00:15:53,571 --> 00:15:58,205
A summer festival? I'd love to!

291
00:15:58,228 --> 00:16:02,664
There's a festival near Asakusa.

292
00:16:02,687 --> 00:16:05,854
Should we wear yukata?

293
00:16:05,877 --> 00:16:10,564
Yeah, I rented one from a kimono shop.

294
00:16:10,587 --> 00:16:12,754
That looks lovely on you!

295
00:16:12,777 --> 00:16:14,777
You look great in it!

296
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:18,202
There'll be so many food stalls!

297
00:16:18,226 --> 00:16:22,118
What kind of food do they sell at the stalls?

298
00:16:22,142 --> 00:16:27,385
Takoyaki, yakisoba, yakitori—you name it!

299
00:16:27,409 --> 00:16:30,864
We can snack as we walk around!

300
00:16:30,887 --> 00:16:33,702
They have goldfish scooping too!

301
00:16:33,726 --> 00:16:36,133
I've seen it on TV!

302
00:16:36,156 --> 00:16:38,290
I want to try it!

303
00:16:38,313 --> 00:16:41,532
You scoop them up with a paper net called a poi.

304
00:16:41,555 --> 00:16:44,824
I'll scoop it up carefully so it doesn't tear.

305
00:16:44,848 --> 00:16:48,614
We also have shooting games and ring toss.

306
00:16:48,637 --> 00:16:51,571
The games look fun too!

307
00:16:51,594 --> 00:16:55,847
When night falls, the lanterns light up.

308
00:16:55,870 --> 00:17:00,003
It's so beautiful and magical.

309
00:17:00,026 --> 00:17:02,605
We also dance Bon Odori.

310
00:17:02,629 --> 00:17:05,478
Can I dance with you?

311
00:17:05,501 --> 00:17:10,034
Yes, everyone is welcome to join!

312
00:17:10,057 --> 00:17:13,024
Could you teach me how to dance?

313
00:17:13,047 --> 00:17:17,247
Just follow along with the hand movements, and you'll be fine.

314
00:17:17,270 --> 00:17:20,737
I can really feel the essence of a Japanese summer.

315
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:23,893
There are spots where you can see fireworks too.

316
00:17:23,916 --> 00:17:27,683
The boom of the fireworks really echoes, doesn't it?

317
00:17:27,706 --> 00:17:32,306
It's a little cooler at night than during the day.

318
00:17:32,329 --> 00:17:35,908
It's going to be a fun night!

319
00:17:35,932 --> 00:17:39,786
Yes, let's make lots of memories.

320
00:17:39,809 --> 00:17:41,775
I'm really looking forward to it!

321
00:17:41,798 --> 00:17:43,932
Let's go soon!

322
00:17:43,955 --> 00:17:45,455
Scene 10: Summer Break Health Management

323
00:17:45,455 --> 00:17:49,553
Is your summer break planning going well?

324
00:17:49,576 --> 00:17:51,309
Yes, it is.

325
00:17:51,332 --> 00:17:54,669
But I'm worried about staying healthy.

326
00:17:54,692 --> 00:17:58,571
It's so hot, so prevention is key.

327
00:17:58,595 --> 00:18:01,843
What kind of things are you careful about?

328
00:18:01,866 --> 00:18:06,000
I make sure to get enough sleep.

329
00:18:06,023 --> 00:18:09,438
Doesn't the heat wake you up at night?

330
00:18:09,462 --> 00:18:14,511
I leave the air conditioner on all night instead of using a timer.

331
00:18:14,534 --> 00:18:17,585
That way, I can sleep better.

332
00:18:17,609 --> 00:18:19,183
Yes, it is.

333
00:18:19,207 --> 00:18:21,641
I can get a deep sleep.

334
00:18:21,664 --> 00:18:25,197
Are you eating breakfast?

335
00:18:25,220 --> 00:18:26,458
Yes, it is.

336
00:18:26,482 --> 00:18:29,658
I have miso soup and a banana.

337
00:18:29,681 --> 00:18:32,915
That helps with salt and hydration.

338
00:18:32,938 --> 00:18:36,419
I don’t push myself when I go out.

339
00:18:36,442 --> 00:18:39,917
If I get tired, I go into a café.

340
00:18:39,940 --> 00:18:41,507
Yes, it is.

341
00:18:41,530 --> 00:18:44,296
I take a break every 30 minutes.

342
00:18:44,319 --> 00:18:48,086
I stay in tune with how my body feels.

343
00:18:48,109 --> 00:18:51,806
My friends and I look out for each other.

344
00:18:51,830 --> 00:18:53,763
Have you had some water?

345
00:18:53,786 --> 00:18:55,519
That’s what we ask each other.

346
00:18:55,542 --> 00:18:57,999
That’s a great way to check in!

347
00:18:58,023 --> 00:19:01,223
I also wear sunscreen.

348
00:19:01,246 --> 00:19:04,413
It helps prevent sunburn.

349
00:19:04,436 --> 00:19:06,769
I wear sunglasses too.

350
00:19:06,792 --> 00:19:10,564
Protecting your eyes is important as well.

351
00:19:10,588 --> 00:19:12,866
You’re perfectly prepared!

352
00:19:12,889 --> 00:19:16,722
I want to enjoy summer while staying healthy.

353
00:19:16,745 --> 00:19:19,184
I’ll follow your example.

354
00:19:19,208 --> 00:19:22,659
Staying healthy makes the best memories.

355
00:19:22,683 --> 00:19:25,016
That’s so true.

356
00:19:25,039 --> 00:19:28,176
Let’s have a safe trip.

357
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:31,855
Thank you for the advice!

358
00:19:31,878 --> 00:19:33,378
Scene 11: Traditional Japanese Ways to Beat the Heat

359
00:19:33,378 --> 00:19:38,945
Have you heard about traditional Japanese ways to stay cool?

360
00:19:38,968 --> 00:19:42,574
You’ve probably heard of *uchimizu*, right?

361
00:19:42,597 --> 00:19:46,874
*Uchimizu* is such a clever idea.

362
00:19:46,898 --> 00:19:50,631
You just sprinkle water on the ground.

363
00:19:50,654 --> 00:19:56,654
Exactly! When the water evaporates, it cools the air.

364
00:19:56,678 --> 00:20:01,483
It works best in the morning or evening.

365
00:20:01,506 --> 00:20:04,473
We also hang wind chimes.

366
00:20:04,496 --> 00:20:07,501
Those glass bells?

367
00:20:07,524 --> 00:20:12,691
When the wind blows, they go *cling*.

368
00:20:12,714 --> 00:20:16,412
The sound makes you feel cooler.

369
00:20:16,435 --> 00:20:21,102
Japanese people even find coolness in sound.

370
00:20:21,125 --> 00:20:23,960
What an elegant culture.

371
00:20:23,983 --> 00:20:27,950
We also use *sudare* and *yoshizu*.

372
00:20:27,973 --> 00:20:31,183
Those bamboo curtains, right?

373
00:20:31,206 --> 00:20:35,485
They create shade and let the breeze through.

374
00:20:35,509 --> 00:20:38,551
Such wisdom from the past.

375
00:20:38,574 --> 00:20:45,941
Yukata are great too—they’re made of breathable cotton.

376
00:20:45,963 --> 00:20:49,566
They absorb sweat really well.

377
00:20:49,590 --> 00:20:52,623
And they look so refreshing.

378
00:20:52,646 --> 00:20:56,822
Even watching goldfish can be cooling.

379
00:20:56,846 --> 00:21:00,413
Their smooth, gliding movements.

380
00:21:00,436 --> 00:21:03,869
It puts you in a relaxed, cool mood.

381
00:21:03,892 --> 00:21:07,859
It’s all about living in harmony with nature.

382
00:21:07,882 --> 00:21:11,687
These were clever ways to stay cool before air conditioning.

383
00:21:11,710 --> 00:21:16,344
And they’re still useful today!

384
00:21:16,367 --> 00:21:19,818
I’ll try hanging wind chimes at home.

385
00:21:19,842 --> 00:21:21,928
The sound is so nice.

386
00:21:21,952 --> 00:21:24,051
It’s really soothing.

387
00:21:24,074 --> 00:21:28,208
Enjoy a traditional Japanese summer!

388
00:21:28,231 --> 00:21:31,598
I am—it’s wonderful!

389
00:21:31,621 --> 00:21:33,121
Scene 12: How to Enjoy Summer Resorts

390
00:21:33,121 --> 00:21:37,088
It’s so hot—why don’t we escape to a summer resort?

391
00:21:37,111 --> 00:21:39,277
A summer resort?

392
00:21:39,300 --> 00:21:41,769
Where’s a good spot?

393
00:21:41,793 --> 00:21:45,260
Karuizawa is really popular.

394
00:21:45,283 --> 00:21:47,963
That’s in Nagano, right?

395
00:21:47,986 --> 00:21:51,786
It’s in the mountains, so it’s nice and cool.

396
00:21:51,809 --> 00:21:55,342
Can we get there by Shinkansen from Tokyo?

397
00:21:55,365 --> 00:21:58,816
Yes, it’s just an hour away!

398
00:21:58,839 --> 00:22:01,440
That’s so close!

399
00:22:01,464 --> 00:22:04,916
There are stylish shops and cafés too.

400
00:22:04,939 --> 00:22:07,818
Can we rent bicycles?

401
00:22:07,842 --> 00:22:13,127
Riding through the forest feels amazing.

402
00:22:13,151 --> 00:22:15,517
The sunlight filtering through the trees looks so pretty.

403
00:22:15,540 --> 00:22:18,628
There’s also Shiraito Falls.

404
00:22:18,651 --> 00:22:21,855
Is it cool near the waterfall?

405
00:22:21,879 --> 00:22:25,412
It’s full of negative ions—so refreshing!

406
00:22:25,435 --> 00:22:29,729
Oku-Nikko in Nikko is cool too.

407
00:22:29,752 --> 00:22:32,686
It’s at a high elevation, right?

408
00:22:32,709 --> 00:22:36,242
There are lakes and marshes here.

409
00:22:36,265 --> 00:22:38,998
Perfect for hiking, isn’t it?

410
00:22:39,021 --> 00:22:41,555
And there are plenty of waterfalls too.

411
00:22:41,578 --> 00:22:45,434
Kegon Falls is absolutely breathtaking.

412
00:22:45,457 --> 00:22:48,866
A cool breeze is blowing—so refreshing!

413
00:22:48,889 --> 00:22:51,856
The hotels and pensions here are so stylish.

414
00:22:51,879 --> 00:22:54,846
You can enjoy delicious fresh vegetables.

415
00:22:54,868 --> 00:22:58,047
Summer in the highlands is the best!

416
00:22:58,071 --> 00:23:01,137
I want to go this weekend!

417
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:03,571
Let’s book the tickets.

418
00:23:03,595 --> 00:23:06,795
Sure, I’ll look it up right away.

419
00:23:06,818 --> 00:23:08,318
Scene 13: River Fun and Rafting Adventure

420
00:23:08,318 --> 00:23:12,057
Have you ever played in a river before?

421
00:23:12,080 --> 00:23:16,213
Yeah, I did when I was little.

422
00:23:16,236 --> 00:23:19,613
You can try rafting here!

423
00:23:19,637 --> 00:23:23,004
You mean riding down the river in an inflatable boat?

424
00:23:23,027 --> 00:23:24,693
Yes, it is.

425
00:23:24,716 --> 00:23:27,750
The water splashes on you—so refreshing!

426
00:23:27,773 --> 00:23:30,043
That sounds like fun!

427
00:23:30,066 --> 00:23:32,599
Where can we do it?

428
00:23:32,622 --> 00:23:35,674
You can do it in Nagatoro, Saitama.

429
00:23:35,698 --> 00:23:39,384
Can we go there and back from Tokyo in a day?

430
00:23:39,408 --> 00:23:42,982
It’s about a two-hour train ride.

431
00:23:43,005 --> 00:23:46,938
Will a guide ride with us?

432
00:23:46,961 --> 00:23:50,648
A professional guide will be there to instruct us.

433
00:23:50,672 --> 00:23:53,605
We’ll wear life jackets too, right?

434
00:23:53,628 --> 00:23:57,161
Safety measures are thorough.

435
00:23:57,184 --> 00:24:00,318
Do we go down rough rapids?

436
00:24:00,341 --> 00:24:03,797
There’s a beginner-friendly course.

437
00:24:03,820 --> 00:24:07,420
That makes me feel at ease!

438
00:24:07,443 --> 00:24:10,579
You can even jump into the river!

439
00:24:10,602 --> 00:24:14,169
The water must feel amazing—so cool and refreshing!

440
00:24:14,192 --> 00:24:16,044
Yes, it is.

441
00:24:16,067 --> 00:24:18,467
It feels absolutely incredible!

442
00:24:18,490 --> 00:24:21,362
I’ll bring a change of clothes.

443
00:24:21,386 --> 00:24:25,285
You’ll need clothes and shoes that can get wet.

444
00:24:25,309 --> 00:24:28,587
I’ll wear sandals that won’t come off when wet.

445
00:24:28,610 --> 00:24:32,177
The guide will even take photos for us!

446
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:35,133
That’ll make such great memories!

447
00:24:35,156 --> 00:24:38,629
We can even hit an onsen on the way back.

448
00:24:38,653 --> 00:24:42,220
A hot spring after all that fun sounds perfect!

449
00:24:42,243 --> 00:24:46,082
It’s a must-try summer activity!

450
00:24:46,106 --> 00:24:48,708
I definitely want to give it a try!

451
00:24:48,731 --> 00:24:50,231
Scene 14: A Stroll Through the Department Store Basement

452
00:24:50,231 --> 00:24:54,504
Let’s cool off while we shop.

453
00:24:54,528 --> 00:24:57,061
Where should we go?

454
00:24:57,084 --> 00:25:00,857
Let’s head to the basement of a department store in Shinjuku.

455
00:25:00,881 --> 00:25:03,778
Is it cool down there?

456
00:25:03,801 --> 00:25:07,601
The air conditioning is strong—it’s nice and cool.

457
00:25:07,624 --> 00:25:11,158
There are so many shops!

458
00:25:11,181 --> 00:25:14,864
You’ll find famous Japanese and Western sweets.

459
00:25:14,887 --> 00:25:18,820
Do they sell side dishes and bento boxes too?

460
00:25:18,843 --> 00:25:23,216
Wow, look at all these delicious deli dishes!

461
00:25:23,240 --> 00:25:27,410
Just looking at them gets me excited!

462
00:25:27,433 --> 00:25:31,836
Taking the underground walkway means we won’t get wet.

463
00:25:31,859 --> 00:25:35,118
There’s no sunlight down here, is there?

464
00:25:35,141 --> 00:25:38,548
It’s so convenient—directly connected to the station!

465
00:25:38,571 --> 00:25:41,505
And it’s nice and cool for walking around.

466
00:25:41,528 --> 00:25:45,295
Tokyo Station’s underground area is huge, too!

467
00:25:45,318 --> 00:25:48,403
Oh, there’s a character shop here!

468
00:25:48,427 --> 00:25:51,082
You can buy anime merchandise here.

469
00:25:51,105 --> 00:25:54,785
I’m looking for souvenirs for my friends.

470
00:25:54,809 --> 00:25:58,495
If we get tired, we can relax at an underground café.

471
00:25:58,518 --> 00:26:02,610
I’ll grab an iced coffee—perfect for cooling down.

472
00:26:02,634 --> 00:26:05,271
Shopping down here is so comfortable.

473
00:26:05,295 --> 00:26:08,773
It makes you forget how hot it is outside!

474
00:26:08,796 --> 00:26:12,289
Let’s pick up dinner on the way home.

475
00:26:12,313 --> 00:26:15,513
I’ll get some tasty deli food.

476
00:26:15,536 --> 00:26:18,348
We can enjoy it at home where it’s nice and cool.

477
00:26:18,371 --> 00:26:22,337
What a fantastic way to spend the day!

478
00:26:22,360 --> 00:26:23,860
Scene 15: Enjoying Summer Fruits – A Taste of Japan’s Seasonal Delights

479
00:26:23,860 --> 00:26:28,231
Japanese summer fruits are so delicious, aren’t they?

480
00:26:28,255 --> 00:26:31,113
Have you tried watermelon yet?

481
00:26:31,137 --> 00:26:35,070
Yes, I had some chilled watermelon.

482
00:26:35,093 --> 00:26:38,584
It’s so juicy and refreshing!

483
00:26:38,608 --> 00:26:42,775
A little salt really brings out the sweetness.

484
00:26:42,798 --> 00:26:45,564
Wait—you put salt on it?

485
00:26:45,587 --> 00:26:47,821
That’s surprising!

486
00:26:47,844 --> 00:26:50,610
It really enhances the flavor!

487
00:26:50,633 --> 00:26:53,233
I’ll have to try that next time.

488
00:26:53,256 --> 00:26:56,262
Peaches are in season now, too.

489
00:26:56,285 --> 00:26:59,159
Are those Yamanashi peaches?

490
00:26:59,183 --> 00:27:03,452
Yes, they’re so soft and juicy!

491
00:27:03,476 --> 00:27:06,409
And they smell so sweet!

492
00:27:06,432 --> 00:27:10,232
Hokkaido is famous for its melons, too.

493
00:27:10,255 --> 00:27:12,822
You mean Yubari melons?

494
00:27:12,845 --> 00:27:16,678
They have that beautiful orange flesh and are so sweet!

495
00:27:16,701 --> 00:27:19,678
They’re such a luxury fruit.

496
00:27:19,701 --> 00:27:23,268
A lot of people give them as gifts.

497
00:27:23,291 --> 00:27:25,926
And now grapes are in season!

498
00:27:25,950 --> 00:27:28,588
Shine Muscat grapes, right?

499
00:27:28,611 --> 00:27:31,885
You can eat them with the skin on!

500
00:27:31,908 --> 00:27:34,587
They’re seedless and so sweet!

501
00:27:34,611 --> 00:27:37,878
They’re one of my favorite fruits!

502
00:27:37,901 --> 00:27:40,540
You can find them at supermarkets.

503
00:27:40,564 --> 00:27:43,697
I’ll chill them in the fridge before eating.

504
00:27:43,720 --> 00:27:46,963
They’re packed with vitamins—so healthy!

505
00:27:46,986 --> 00:27:50,386
Summer fruits are one of the best parts of the season!

506
00:27:50,409 --> 00:27:54,303
Let’s enjoy plenty of delicious fruit this summer!

507
00:27:54,327 --> 00:27:57,930
Yes, I’ll go buy some today!

508
00:27:57,953 --> 00:27:59,453
Scene 16: Beach Day Essentials – Tips for a Fun & Safe Sea Swim

509
00:27:59,453 --> 00:28:02,631
Want to go swimming at the beach?

510
00:28:02,654 --> 00:28:05,421
Where should we go to the beach?

511
00:28:05,444 --> 00:28:08,335
Let's head to Shonan Beach!

512
00:28:08,359 --> 00:28:11,559
Are there any beach huts?

513
00:28:11,582 --> 00:28:15,834
Yes, you can change clothes and take showers there.

514
00:28:15,857 --> 00:28:19,590
We can grab ramen or curry too, right?

515
00:28:19,613 --> 00:28:23,454
Curry by the sea tastes amazing!

516
00:28:23,478 --> 00:28:27,244
Are there any rules for swimming?

517
00:28:27,267 --> 00:28:31,351
Don’t swim in areas where it’s prohibited.

518
00:28:31,374 --> 00:28:35,008
Follow the lifeguard’s instructions.

519
00:28:35,031 --> 00:28:38,831
Always check the flag colors.

520
00:28:38,854 --> 00:28:41,820
Red flags mean danger, right?

521
00:28:41,843 --> 00:28:46,413
Yes, we’ll swim when the flag is blue.

522
00:28:46,437 --> 00:28:49,370
We should also watch out for jellyfish.

523
00:28:49,393 --> 00:28:53,596
Jellyfish numbers increase from mid-August.

524
00:28:53,620 --> 00:28:56,420
Wearing a rash guard helps.

525
00:28:56,443 --> 00:28:59,538
It also protects against sunburn!

526
00:28:59,561 --> 00:29:02,328
Let’s take our trash home with us.

527
00:29:02,351 --> 00:29:05,485
Let’s keep the beach clean and beautiful.

528
00:29:05,509 --> 00:29:09,442
Swimming after drinking alcohol is a no-go.

529
00:29:09,465 --> 00:29:13,759
Yes, it’s really dangerous.

530
00:29:13,782 --> 00:29:16,880
Let’s swim safely and have fun!

531
00:29:16,904 --> 00:29:20,342
Just listening to the sound of the waves is so relaxing.

532
00:29:20,365 --> 00:29:23,569
The sea breeze feels great, doesn’t it?

533
00:29:23,593 --> 00:29:26,606
Let’s get ready and head out!

534
00:29:26,630 --> 00:29:29,596
Don’t forget to bring your swimsuit!

535
00:29:29,619 --> 00:29:31,119
Scene 17: Introduction to Glamping

536
00:29:31,119 --> 00:29:34,753
Have you ever been camping?

537
00:29:34,776 --> 00:29:37,791
No, but I’d love to try it!

538
00:29:37,814 --> 00:29:40,847
I recommend glamping!

539
00:29:40,870 --> 00:29:43,278
Glamping?

540
00:29:43,301 --> 00:29:45,139
What’s that?

541
00:29:45,163 --> 00:29:49,196
It’s camping with all the gear already set up for you.

542
00:29:49,219 --> 00:29:52,153
So, we don’t have to pitch a tent?

543
00:29:52,176 --> 00:29:56,209
Exactly! There’s already a luxurious tent ready.

544
00:29:56,232 --> 00:29:59,599
Are there beds and air conditioning too?

545
00:29:59,621 --> 00:30:03,655
Yes, it’s as comfortable as a hotel!

546
00:30:03,678 --> 00:30:07,244
That sounds perfect for beginners!

547
00:30:07,267 --> 00:30:11,562
They even provide barbecue ingredients.

548
00:30:11,586 --> 00:30:14,719
We can grill meat and veggies to eat.

549
00:30:14,742 --> 00:30:17,476
It’s so easy—you can go empty-handed!

550
00:30:17,499 --> 00:30:19,832
Where can we find glamping sites?

551
00:30:19,855 --> 00:30:23,622
There are some near Mt. Fuji and in Chiba.

552
00:30:23,645 --> 00:30:27,078
Can we see the stars clearly at night?

553
00:30:27,101 --> 00:30:31,359
Yes, the surroundings are dark, so the stars are stunning.

554
00:30:31,382 --> 00:30:34,382
We can even do some stargazing!

555
00:30:34,405 --> 00:30:38,205
Gathering around a campfire to chat is so much fun.

556
00:30:38,228 --> 00:30:41,202
I want to make s’mores!

557
00:30:41,226 --> 00:30:44,393
They’re delicious when sandwiched in crackers.

558
00:30:44,416 --> 00:30:46,695
S’mores, you mean?

559
00:30:46,718 --> 00:30:48,685
I love them!

560
00:30:48,708 --> 00:30:52,521
The morning air is so refreshing.

561
00:30:52,545 --> 00:30:56,022
We enjoy breakfast in the heart of nature.

562
00:30:56,045 --> 00:30:59,142
It's a luxurious way to spend your time.

563
00:30:59,165 --> 00:31:02,498
I'd love to book this for my next day off.

564
00:31:02,521 --> 00:31:04,021
Scene 18: The Allure of Night Pools

565
00:31:04,021 --> 00:31:07,555
Have you ever heard of night pools?

566
00:31:07,578 --> 00:31:10,746
You mean swimming in a pool at night?

567
00:31:10,770 --> 00:31:15,103
You can swim in hotel pools after dark.

568
00:31:15,126 --> 00:31:18,301
They're popular because you won’t get sunburned.

569
00:31:18,324 --> 00:31:22,411
Yes, and they’re beautifully lit up.

570
00:31:22,435 --> 00:31:26,238
Do they have a DJ playing music?

571
00:31:26,262 --> 00:31:29,934
Stylish music fills the air.

572
00:31:29,957 --> 00:31:33,390
You can take amazing photos there.

573
00:31:33,413 --> 00:31:36,691
The floaties come in cute designs too.

574
00:31:36,715 --> 00:31:40,689
Can you get drinks there?

575
00:31:40,712 --> 00:31:44,170
You can enjoy cocktails and juice.

576
00:31:44,193 --> 00:31:46,660
It has such a sophisticated vibe.

577
00:31:46,683 --> 00:31:50,616
Luxury hotels in Tokyo offer this experience.

578
00:31:50,639 --> 00:31:53,639
Is it cooler than during the day?

579
00:31:53,662 --> 00:31:57,149
It’s much cooler without the sun.

580
00:31:57,173 --> 00:32:00,306
You could even go after work.

581
00:32:00,329 --> 00:32:03,331
They also offer swimsuit rentals.

582
00:32:03,354 --> 00:32:06,354
It’s so easy to drop by.

583
00:32:06,377 --> 00:32:09,744
Let’s go swimming with friends.

584
00:32:09,767 --> 00:32:13,051
Do we need a reservation?

585
00:32:13,075 --> 00:32:17,008
You pay online in advance.

586
00:32:17,031 --> 00:32:19,598
The tickets are really popular.

587
00:32:19,621 --> 00:32:23,266
You can immerse yourself in a magical world.

588
00:32:23,289 --> 00:32:26,723
It’s the perfect escape from everyday life.

589
00:32:26,746 --> 00:32:30,079
It’ll be a wonderful summer night.

590
00:32:30,102 --> 00:32:33,001
Let’s go check it out!

591
00:32:33,024 --> 00:32:34,524
Scene 19: Summer Ghost Stories and Their Cooling Power

592
00:32:34,524 --> 00:32:39,814
In Japan, we have a tradition of telling scary stories in the summer.

593
00:32:39,838 --> 00:32:44,642
Why do we tell scary stories in the summer?

594
00:32:44,666 --> 00:32:48,633
Because they give you chills and cool you down.

595
00:32:48,656 --> 00:32:51,589
That’s such a fun reason!

596
00:32:51,612 --> 00:32:55,346
Haunted houses are also really popular.

597
00:32:55,368 --> 00:32:58,902
You mean like the haunted houses at amusement parks?

598
00:32:58,925 --> 00:33:02,858
Fuji-Q Highland is famous for them.

599
00:33:02,881 --> 00:33:06,060
There’s even a haunted hospital attraction.

600
00:33:06,084 --> 00:33:10,371
It’s so scary you might not be able to walk.

601
00:33:10,394 --> 00:33:15,561
Do real actors perform in them?

602
00:33:15,584 --> 00:33:19,351
Yes, they suddenly appear to scare you.

603
00:33:19,374 --> 00:33:22,670
You’ll definitely scream!

604
00:33:22,693 --> 00:33:25,670
It’ll give you goosebumps.

605
00:33:25,693 --> 00:33:28,865
That *does* sound cooling.

606
00:33:28,889 --> 00:33:32,422
It really has a cooling effect.

607
00:33:32,445 --> 00:33:35,778
Let’s go with friends.

608
00:33:35,801 --> 00:33:38,578
It’ll bring you closer together.

609
00:33:38,602 --> 00:33:41,935
You’ll end up holding hands out of fear!

610
00:33:41,958 --> 00:33:45,692
Traditional ghost stories are fascinating too.

611
00:33:45,715 --> 00:33:48,681
You mean *Yotsuya Kaidan*?

612
00:33:48,704 --> 00:33:52,537
Yes, you can even hear it in *rakugo* performances.

613
00:33:52,560 --> 00:33:55,760
You imagine the story as you listen.

614
00:33:55,783 --> 00:33:58,917
It sends shivers down my spine.

615
00:33:58,940 --> 00:34:02,219
It’s a uniquely summer experience.

616
00:34:02,242 --> 00:34:05,694
Want to give it a try?

617
00:34:05,717 --> 00:34:09,990
It’s a little scary, but I’d love to go.

618
00:34:10,014 --> 00:34:13,308
Let’s muster up the courage and go!

619
00:34:13,332 --> 00:34:14,832
Scene 20: Summer Travel Plans and Safety Tips

620
00:34:14,832 --> 00:34:19,036
Let’s finalize our summer travel plans.

621
00:34:19,060 --> 00:34:22,342
There’s so much I want to do!

622
00:34:22,365 --> 00:34:26,165
We also checked the latest news for reference.

623
00:34:26,188 --> 00:34:29,832
We’ll take heatstroke precautions seriously.

624
00:34:29,856 --> 00:34:34,510
We’ll visit cool indoor attractions and summer retreats.

625
00:34:34,534 --> 00:34:38,510
And of course, we’ll enjoy lots of delicious food.

626
00:34:38,534 --> 00:34:42,310
Staying healthy is the top priority.

627
00:34:42,333 --> 00:34:45,266
We’ll keep the schedule relaxed and manageable.

628
00:34:45,289 --> 00:34:49,256
We won’t forget to hydrate and take breaks.

629
00:34:49,279 --> 00:34:52,857
We’ll carry parasols and portable fans too.

630
00:34:52,880 --> 00:34:56,946
That way, we can safely enjoy Japan’s summer!

631
00:34:56,969 --> 00:34:59,940
We’ll take plenty of great photos too.

632
00:34:59,964 --> 00:35:03,571
It’ll make for wonderful summer memories.

633
00:35:03,595 --> 00:35:06,961
We’ll prepare thoroughly before we leave.

634
00:35:06,984 --> 00:35:10,618
We’ve already booked our transportation in advance.

635
00:35:10,641 --> 00:35:14,041
And we’ve double-checked the hotel reservations.

636
00:35:14,063 --> 00:35:17,297
Have a safe and enjoyable trip!

637
00:35:17,320 --> 00:35:20,586
Thanks for joining in on the fun!

638
00:35:20,609 --> 00:35:23,643
Wishing you an amazing trip!

639
00:35:23,666 --> 00:35:26,466
Yes, I’m off!

640
00:35:26,489 --> 00:35:29,577
Take care and have a great time!